# Copy the Electron entry HTML from frontend/ up into the build variant root
# so the renderer can `loadFile(index.html)` (paths inside index.html are
# resolved relative to the variant root).  `!tup_preserve` copies a source
# file into the variant tree; it works on every platform — Windows included,
# see the resource Tupfiles under public/resources/* — so these rules are no
# longer gated behind `ifneq win32`.  Note the input/output relative paths
# must differ (frontend/index.html -> index.html): a same-relative-path
# `!tup_preserve` from this parent Tupfile triggers a Tup "generated node
# already exists as a normal file" conflict against the variant-mirrored
# source copy.
#
# The default config/layout files are published by a Tupfile of their own,
# `config/Tupfile`, for exactly that reason: a rule whose Tupfile sits in the
# same directory as its inputs has no relative-path clash.  This comment used
# to say they "already reach build-debug/config/ via the variant source
# mirror" and needed no rule.  That was false, and it cost a working `ct`: the
# variant mirror reproduces the source DIRECTORY tree into the variant and
# copies no files, so `build-debug/config/` was created — and stayed empty —
# on every clean build, and `ct` died on first run with an uncaught OSError
# naming `build-debug/config/default_config.yaml`.  See `config/Tupfile` for
# the full account and `scripts/require-runtime-assets.sh` for the guard that
# now makes a regression loud.
: frontend/index.html |> !tup_preserve |> index.html
: frontend/subwindow.html |> !tup_preserve |> subwindow.html
